        "id": "ch12_1_5-1",
        "text": "One-to-many sessions\nWe can also run commands and scripts on multiple machines at once by using the Invoke-Command\ncmdlet, like this:\nInvoke-Command -ComputerName <name 1>, <name 2> -ScriptBlock\n{Get-Service}\nThis will run the commands or scripts in the scriptblock against the list of names specified in the\n-ComputerName parameter. This command uses PowerShell remoting the same as the previous\nPSSession cmdlets.\nBeing able to run commands on remote machines makes PowerShell an extremely useful administration\ntool, which unfortunately means that it is also a security risk. Let\u2019s look now at the ways we can help\nprevent PowerShell from causing problems.",
